  "claim": "The developer of origami technique Wet-folding was given the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, award. The award was given by the man Lee Bong-chang tried to assassinate during the Kenneth B. Pyle era in Japanese history.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Akira Yoshizawa. Sentence: In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded him the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, one of the highest honors bestowed in Japan.\nPage: Hirohito. Sentence: The word \"Shōwa\" is the name of the era that corresponded with the Emperor's reign, and was made the Emperor's own name upon his death.\nPage: Wet-folding. Sentence: Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that employs water to dampen the paper so that it can be manipulated more easily.\nPage: Lee Bong-chang. Sentence: In 1932, he attempted unsuccessfully to assassinate Japanese emperor Hirohito with a hand grenade, which became known as the Sakuradamon Incident.",
