        "original_id": "031ecec4-5520-5c42-a0c7-56b8238e6be8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Hirohito, Lee Bong-chang\n- Concepts: Shōwa, wet-folding\n- Honors: Order of the Rising Sun\n- Events: Sakuradamon Incident\n\nFacts:\n- In 1932, Lee Bong-chang unsuccessfully attempted to assassinate Emperor Hirohito with a hand grenade in the Sakuradamon Incident.\n- Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Shōwa was the era name corresponding to Hirohito's reign and became Hirohito's own name after his death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
